# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Internet Frontend — environment variables
# Copy to .env in this directory.
# All variables must be prefixed with VITE_ to be accessible in the browser bundle.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Backend signaling server URL — as seen FROM THE BROWSER (not from Docker).
#
# Development (leave empty):
#   vite.config.js proxies /socket.io to http://localhost:3001 automatically.
#   Leaving this empty means no URL is hardcoded — the proxy handles routing.
#
# Production (set this):
#   The built JS bundle uses this URL to open the socket.io connection.
#   Must be the full URL including protocol and port if non-standard.
#   Examples:
#     VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://share.yourdomain.com
#     VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://192.168.1.10:3001
VITE_BACKEND_URL=
